  "title": "India's H-1B Visa Fee Extension and Its Impact on the US-India Trade",
  "summary": "The US President Donald Trump extended the H-1B visa fee for a USD 100,000 payment for another year, affecting Indian professionals and students entering the US workforce. This extension is part of a broader political and economic conflict, with India facing challenges due to the administration's policies.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Trump administration extended the H-1B visa fee requirement by a year, making it effective until September 21, 2027.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The extension impacts Indian professionals and students, causing job losses and increased remittances.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "India faces challenges due to the administration's policies, including the H-1B fee.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
